<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uysyn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uysun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uysyn are a tribe of the Senior Jüz of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a>, living in southern and south-eastern Kazakhstan. They were nomadic herders whose pastures lay near the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkistan-city">Turkistan</a>. Their name has often been linked with the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wusun">Wusun</a> people of the same region, though the connection is debated.</p></div>
